# The on-disk opcode cache that serve.sh writes. It is 55 MB of compiled PHP whose paths
# encode the absolute project location, and git refuses some of them as "Filename too long".
# Deleting it costs one slow start and nothing else.
/storage/framework/opcache/
# Backups (§14.14). Both paths are already covered by storage/app/.gitignore (`*`), but
# they are stated explicitly so a future edit to that file cannot silently start committing
# a zip that contains a full database dump. `backup-temp` is the zip staging directory.
# The `local` disk is a development convenience — production must use a remote disk, see
# BACKEND_DEPLOYMENT_GUIDE.md §7.
/storage/app/backup-temp/
/storage/app/private/
/vendor
Homestead.json
Homestead.yaml
Thumbs.db

